 nd founder of MIA ANASA. Since 1997 he has performed throughout New Englan
 d\, including appearances at MIT's Kresge Auditorium\, the Tsai Performanc
 e Center\, and the Maliotis Cultural Center. His original music combines t
 he rich traditions of Greek folk and rebetiko with contemporary influences
 . His latest album\, Meeting Point\, reflects his passion for building cul
 tural bridges through original songs that honor Greek musical heritage whi
 le speaking to today's audiences.\nhttps://tickets.24hourmusic.com/eventpe
 rformances.asp?evt=1902\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https://pushpin.city/
